A code block needs at least one bound variable: {|| ...} and the
whitespace-only {| | ...} do not compile (diag.code_block_structure,
error, ranged on the whole block). {|x| ...} and array literals do not
fire.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Blocks;
	:DECLARE fnConst, fnSpaced, fnDouble, aList;
	fnConst := {|| 42};
	fnSpaced := {| | 42};
	fnDouble := {|x| x * 2};
	aList := {1, 2, 3};
	:RETURN {fnConst, fnSpaced, fnDouble, aList, {}};
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Blocks;
	:DECLARE fnConst, fnSpaced, fnDouble, aList;

	fnConst := {|| 42};
	fnSpaced := {|| 42};
	fnDouble := {|x| x * 2};
	aList := {1, 2, 3};

	:RETURN {fnConst, fnSpaced, fnDouble, aList, {}};
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
3:13-3:20 error code_block_structure: Code blocks require at least one bound variable between the pipes: {|x| expr} - '{|| ...}' does not compile
4:14-4:22 error code_block_structure: Code blocks require at least one bound variable between the pipes: {|x| expr} - '{|| ...}' does not compile
